.TH SYSTEMD-SWAP 8 "SEPTEMBER 2026" "systemd-swap 0.2.0" systemd-swap
.\" disable french spacing
.ss 12 0
.SH NAME
systemd-swap \- Dynamic swap management for zram, zswap, and swap files.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B systemd-swap
.RB [ \-\-dry\-run ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.RB [ \-V | \-\-version ]
.I start|status|autoconfig
.SH DESCRIPTION
systemd-swap is a daemon started by
.B systemd-swap.service
at boot. It runs a pool of
.B zram
devices that grows as compression saves RAM and shrinks when idle, or
.B zswap
in front of disk swap, and creates preallocated swap files when memory runs
short. The swap mode and its tuning come from
.BR swap.conf (5);
auto mode picks them from the hardware.
.SH COMMANDS
.IP start
Set up swap and keep managing it until SIGTERM. Run by the service unit.
Stopping the service ends the daemon but leaves its swap active, so no page
has to come back into RAM; the next start adopts that swap, and at shutdown
systemd deactivates it.
.IP status
Print the status of systemd-swap; modules being used and their statuses.
.IP autoconfig
Print the recommended configuration for the current system without applying it.
.SH OPTIONS
.IP \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be done without mutating system state. No
.BR modprobe (8),
.BR swapon (8),
.BR swapoff (8),
sysfs writes, or
.BR fstab (5)
modifications are performed. Compatible with
.BR start .
Exits 0 on a successful plan.
.IP "\-h, \-\-help"
Print help and exit.
.IP "\-V, \-\-version"
Print version and exit.
